          "eurlex_url": null,
          "retrieval_score": 0.42424244
        }
      ],
      "rationale": "The product is given a legal name, 'Chickpea dip with sesame paste', which is a descriptive name and not just a brand or fancy name. This satisfies the first requirement. For the second requirement, a quantitative indication (QUID) is required for ingredients that appear in the name, are emphasised, or are essential to characterise the food. The ingredients list provides percentages for 'Chickpeas' (54%) and 'SESAME paste' (7%), both of which are in the legal name and/or are emphasised (SESAME paste is in uppercase). This satisfies the QUID requirement.",
